[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/6","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/6/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/6/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/6/events","html_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/6","id":5355801513,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTGQNOc8AAAABCSzN5g","number":6,"title":"docs(training): clarify max-iters as smoke-test option","user":{"login":"cjsj166","id":94033188,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZrVJA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94033188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166","html_url":"https://github.com/cjsj166","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-05T05:18:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T06:26:19Z","closed_at":"2026-09-05T06:21:21Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pulls/6","html_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/6.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Why\n\n`--max-iters` can make the meaning of an epoch ambiguous because it overrides the number of optimizer steps and cycles the loader independently of dataset size. It exists only to run quick smoke tests of the training pipeline and should not be treated as a normal training control.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Marked `max_iters` as smoke-test-only in the training function documentation.\n- Updated the CLI help to explain that real training should leave it unset so one epoch remains one full loader pass.\n\n## Verification\n\nConfirmed that `uv run scripts/train_unet_transformer.py --help` displays the revised `--max-iters` guidance.\n","closed_by":{"login":"cjsj166","id":94033188,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZrVJA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94033188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166","html_url":"https://github.com/cjsj166","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/6/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/6/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/5","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/5/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/5/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/issues/5/events","html_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/5","id":5348355459,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTGQNOc8AAAABCM3WvQ","number":5,"title":"feat(training): log validation metrics to TensorBoard","user":{"login":"cjsj166","id":94033188,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZrVJA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94033188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166","html_url":"https://github.com/cjsj166","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjsj166/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-04T12:59:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T13:13:37Z","closed_at":"2026-09-04T13:13:36Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pulls/5","html_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/5","diff_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/5.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/royerlab/kaggle-cell-tracking-competition/pull/5.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Why\n\nTraining only exposed per-step training losses, while epoch validation returned an edge-loss proxy, accuracy, and node recall without writing them to TensorBoard. This made it difficult to detect overfitting or choose a checkpoint using the competition-relevant behavior, especially division quality and the node over-detection adjustment.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Compute validation edge loss, detection loss, and their weighted combined loss on every epoch.\n- Run full-video graph inference for every validation dataset and evaluate it with the competition metric implementation.\n- Write the combined score, raw and adjusted edge Jaccard, division Jaccard, node recall, edge/division TP/FP/FN counts, predicted and estimated node totals, node-count ratio/adjustment, and over-detection penalty to TensorBoard.\n- Keep per-step training loss logging, per-epoch resumable checkpoints, canonical single-/multi-GPU state handling, and documented resume/TensorBoard commands.\n- Add focused tests covering all three validation losses, full graph metric aggregation, the over-detection penalty, and emitted TensorBoard tags.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `uv run --no-sync pytest -q -m 'not slow'`: 125 passed, 1 slow training integration test deselected.\n- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_training_validation_logging.py`: 3 passed, exercising validation loss calculation, graph metrics, and TensorBoard tag 